tasks.description:
Add the building blocks only, with nothing wired in yet.

(1) In `BankStatementReviewLogic.scala` add:
- a `Loadable[+T]` enum: `Loading`, `Loaded(value: T)`, `Failed(message: String)`, with small helpers such as `toOption` and `map`;
- `final case class ReviewSupport(merchants, categories, rules: List[ImportRuleMatcher.Rule], expenses)`, plus `withRule(rule)`, `withMerchant(m)` and `withExpenses(list)`;
- pure row helpers `patchRow(rows, rowId)(f)` and `replaceRow(rows, fresh)`.

(2) Create `web/src/main/scala/net/wiringbits/components/pages/BankStatementReviewStore.scala`, a plain final class (not a component) that takes an implicit/using `monix.execution.Scheduler`. It exposes:
- `$statement: Var[Loadable[GetBankStatement.Response]]` (metadata, never mutated after Loaded);
- `$rows: Var[List[StatementRowData]]`;
- `$support: Var[Loadable[ReviewSupport]]`;
- `$suggestions: Var[Option[AiSuggestions]]`.

Its methods:
- `statementLoaded(resp)` seeds `$statement`, `$rows` and `$suggestions` together;
- `statementFailed(msg)` and `supportLoaded`/`supportFailed`;
- `updateRows(f)` and `patchRow(rowId)(f)`;
- `updateSupport(f)`, a no-op unless Loaded;
- `setSuggestions(s)`.

Implement updates as `v := f(v())`. JS is single-threaded, so this is safe.

Tests:
- extend `BankStatementReviewLogicSpec` for `patchRow`/`replaceRow`, the `ReviewSupport` helpers and `Loadable`;
- add `BankStatementReviewStoreSpec` using `Scheduler.trampoline()`. Cover: `statementLoaded` seeds all three Vars; `patchRow` touches only the target row; `updateSupport` is ignored while Loading; `setSuggestions` emits nothing on `$rows`/`$statement` (subscribe and count emissions).

Verify with `CI=true sbt Test/compile` and `sbt "web/testOnly *BankStatementReviewLogicSpec *BankStatementReviewStoreSpec"`.
